__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
# This repo is the SYSTEM, not the account. Nothing that belongs to a live
# account goes in it - no settings database, no trade log, no balances, no
# positions. Cloning it must give a clean install and nothing about whoever
# ran the last one.
#
# The full archive - database, log and all - is what backup.py writes to the
# local backup folder every evening. That is where account state is kept.
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
data/holdout_bars/
logs/
snapshot/
_probe_*.py
.env
.pytest_cache/
.pytest_tmp/
.pytest_tmp*/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.url
.vscode/
# Ajan koprüsü: brief'ler, cevaplar, olcum scriptleri ve oturum kancalari.
# Bunlar CALISMA malzemesi, urun degil - depoyu klonlayan biri MicoFX'i
# kurmak istiyor, bizim hangi ajana ne yazdigimizi degil. Hepsi ayni sinif,
# hepsi disarida.
.claude/
claude/*
.cursor/
cursor/*
chatgpt/
antigravity/*
.bridge/
.codex/
CLAUDE_ONERILERI.md

# ...with one exception. The three bridge WATCHERS are not working material,
# they are long-running infrastructure on the operator's machine: each polls a
# mailbox and emits a wake token, and a duplicate of any of them doubles every
# wake. That class of bug cost a morning on 11.09 (three watchers on one leg,
# one of them corrupting a state file) and none of the three had ever been
# reviewable, because the folders they live in were ignored wholesale. The
# messages stay out; the code that runs stays in.
#
# Note the patterns above are "dir/*" rather than "dir/": git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so a "!" line under "claude/"
# would have silently done nothing.
!claude/session_watch.ps1
!cursor/watch_bridges.ps1
!antigravity/WATCH.ps1
# Google Drive masaustu istemcisi bu iki klasoru senkronladigi her klasorde
# acar. Depoda isleri yok; git status onlarla kirlenmesin.
.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp.drivedownload/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/

cookies.txt
_opt_*.json
_poll_opt.*
_restart.json

# Git-bash altinda "2>nul" yazilinca Windows`un bos aygiti yerine bu adda
# gercek bir dosya olusuyor ve icine uyarilar dokuluyor. Urun degil, kaza.
nul

# An inline bridge watcher writes its state file with Set-Content's arguments
# swapped: the hash becomes the FILE NAME and the state path becomes the
# contents. Five landed at the repo root on 10.09 and one reached a commit. I
# wrote here on 10.09 that Cursor had fixed it - wrong: another appeared 11.09
# 08:2x from a freshly armed watcher. It was swept, not fixed. The repo's own
# leg is claude/session_watch.ps1 now, which names every parameter and takes a
# mutex; the pattern stays as a net until nothing arms an inline one, because
# the failure is silent and produces a 64-character file nobody recognises.
# Pinned by tests/test_every_bridge_watcher_is_single_instance.py.
[0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F]*[0-9A-F]
